ATTRIBUTION IN PUBLISHED OUTPUT
-------------------------------
Every report this software publishes carries an attribution line:

    Gold-Dollar-Monitor · github.com/zorgoros/Gold-Dollar-Monitor

It is defined in `src/market_monitor/domain/constants.py` (ATTRIBUTION) and a
test asserts its presence, so removing it takes a deliberate code change that
breaks the test suite.

If you run this software, or a fork of it, and publish its reports, please keep
that line. Operators who want their own channel named in the footer should set
`[reporting].channel_note` in `config/default.toml` — it is added above the
attribution, not instead of it.

This is a request, not a licence condition. The MIT licence permits removal,
and no open-source licence can prevent it. It is asked in good faith.

